# DotApp Error Handling

Full contract: `AIRULES/18-ERROR-HANDLING-AND-RETURN-VALUES.md`.

## Four failure styles

| Style | Where | Handling |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Callback pair | `execute()`, `Entity::save()/delete()`, `DB::schema()` | pass **both** callbacks |
| `false` / `null` | `Crypto::decrypt`→`false`, `Cache::load`→`null`, `Auth::login`→`false`, `Config` getters→`null` | compare explicitly |
| Envelope array | `HttpHelper::request`, `FastSearch::*` | check `['success']` |
| Exceptions | AI (`AIException`), QueryBuilder build, SchemaBuilder, `Auth::createUser`, `DI::resolve` | `try/catch` — `raw()` `?` in comments counts as a placeholder |

## Hard rules

1. `execute()` **without** an error callback **throws** — always pass both. Persist handlers **MUST** also sit in `try/catch` (`\Throwable`).
2. Never bare `->first()`: RAW warns on empty, ORM is fatal. Use `all()` + `[0] ?? null` or `exists()`.
3. `$execution_data` is **empty on a cache hit** → `$exec['insert_id'] ?? $db->inserted_id()`.
4. `Crypto::decrypt()` → `=== false` check.
5. `Cache::load()` → `!== null` check.
6. `Email::send()` returns **`string[]`** on failure → `!== true` check.
7. `Validator::validate()` → `=== true` check (failure array is truthy).
8. `$request->form()` may return your value, `false`, `null`, or **throw** → give it an error callback and guard.
9. Persist / passwords / HTML / URLs: `$request->data(true)` — never `$request->data()`. SQL write = named bindings. Show login `reply.message` on every failure.
10. Missing view/layout renders **`""`** with only a log warning → use the fallback argument and check for `''`.
11. `Entity::save()` returns **void** — never test it.
12. `trigger()` ignores listener return values; listener exceptions propagate.
13. Never write an empty `catch {}`. Log with `Logger::use()->error(...)` and return a structured error.
14. **Catch bus (MUST):** every `catch` **and** every `execute()` `$err` reports `dotapp.catch` then `dotapp.catch.error|info`. Reporting is **extra** — the user still gets the toast. Helper + listener live in **your** module, never under `app/modules/DACore/`.

## Catch bus (`AIRULES/18` §9)

| Event | When |
|-------|------|
| `dotapp.catch` | **failures** — the funnel a debugger subscribes to for `operation`/`source`/`message` |
| `dotapp.catch.error` | the operation aborted |
| `dotapp.catch.info` | expected / recovered (fallback, retry, ignored duplicate) |
| `dotapp.catchall` | **core**, every `trigger()` except itself — event tracer in **your** module. Listener: `($result, $eventname, ...$data)`. Do not fire it yourself. Never under `app/modules/DACore/`. (`AIRULES/01`, `AIRULES/23` §1c) |
| `module.{mod}.{name}.hook` | **owner** after a useful side-effect — names + payload in that module’s `.hooks`. Distinct from catch/catchall. (`AIRULES/41`) |

Fixed payload keys: `severity`, `module`, `source` (`Shop:Items@save`), `operation` (`shop.item.update`), `message`, `exception`, `code`, `file`, `line`, `time` + `context` (ids/counts), `user_id`. **No** passwords, tokens, 2FA codes, decrypted secrets, rights blobs, request bodies or personal data. `trace` only for `error`, only if wanted.

Write **one** report helper per module and call it from every `catch` / `$err` — listener exceptions propagate, so wrap the two `trigger()` calls in the helper’s own `try/catch` and log a broken listener instead of losing the real error. A `dotapp.catch` listener **MUST NOT** push a DACore inbox notification per failure (flood) — use a rate-limited threshold.

## Template

Full skeleton with every stop: `AIRULES/26-CONTROL-SLICE.md` §7. The action answers HTTP **200** on every branch — HTTP 4xx/5xx skips `.after()` and the `load()` success callback, so the message would never reach the toast.

```php
try {
    // Prefix #DACore:AuthTest@LoginAndCRC! already burned the CRC — no crcCheck() here.
    $answer = $request->form(['POST'], 'saveItem', function ($request) {
        return self::saveItem($request->data(true)['data'] ?? []);   // Reply::ok() / Reply::fail()
    }, function ($request, $name) {
        return Reply::fail('This form has expired. Reload the page and try again.');
    });
    if ($answer === false || $answer === null) {
        return Reply::fail('This form does not match its handler (saveItem). Reload the page and try again.');
    }
    return $answer;
} catch (\Throwable $e) {
    // Report first (debugger trail), then answer the user — never leak $e.
    self::reportCatch('Shop:Items@save', 'shop.item.update', $e, 'error', ['item_id' => $id]);
    return Reply::fail('The item was not saved because of a server fault (shop.item.update). The fault was logged.');
}
```

`Reply::ok($message, $extra)` / `Reply::fail($message, $errors)` = your module `Libraries/Reply.php` → `ajaxReply([...], 200)`. Every stop has its own sentence; **MUST NOT** `Server error` / `Bad request` / `Rejected` / `Save failed`. `crcCheck()` returns `1` / `0` / `false` — never compare it with `=== true`.

`reportCatch()` = your module helper: builds the payload, `Events::trigger('dotapp.catch', $p)`, `Events::trigger('dotapp.catch.' . $severity, $p)`, then `Logger::use()->error(...)` (`info` → `warning`, because `info` is dropped by default).

## Broken — do not enable

`Renderer::useCache(true)`, `Config::db('cache', true)` with ORM, `DB::migrate()`, `Auth::hasRole()`, `Auth::logged()`, `Injector::bind/singleton`, `Router::hasRoute()` (inverted).
